# L1 Interference Pre-Edit Screening Prompt

## Job

Screen a document for English phrasing shaped by the author's native
language(s), before detailed editing begins. Scan the entire text, flag
interference by category and severity, and produce a diagnostic summary that
tells the full language edit where to focus.

**Before scanning: if the author's native language(s) have not been stated for
this run, ask which language(s) apply and wait for the answer.** This is the
first thing to check, before reading the document for interference patterns —
see *Guardrails → When to stop and ask* for how to handle multiple languages
or a partial answer. Do not scan against a generic or assumed interference
profile in the meantime.

This runs as an early screening pass, ahead of the detailed language edit
(LANG_EVAL / ESL Fluency & Register Audit). It identifies *where* and *what
kind* of L1 interference is present so the later pass can prioritise; it does
not itself perform the line-level correction that pass carries out.

